cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite both the paper and the dataset using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "AAPF Validation Dataset: Cross-Page-Size ESE Format Changes in Windows Server 2025 and Windows 11"
abstract: >-
  Companion artifacts for the paper "Silent Evidence Loss in Modern Windows: A Detectable Class of Version-Gated Format Change and Its ESE Instance"
  (Forensic Science International: Digital Investigation, 2026). Includes:
  (a) source-level patches for libesedb that resolve the Windows Server 2025 /
  Windows 11 24H2 itagState reinterpretation failures spanning 4 KiB, 16 KiB
  and 32 KiB pages with a single format-revision-gated patch (a no-op by
  construction on databases below the gate; an equivalent fix is in upstream
  libesedb release 20260704);
  (b) a Rust-based NTDS.dit analysis tool (Poneglyph v0.2.3) incorporating the
  patch, plus the Fix 2 ablation pair used in the paper;
  (c) 22 ESE database samples (ntds.dit, DataStore.edb, WebCacheV01.dat,
  SRUDB.dat) populated under the Automated Artifact Population Framework on
  Windows Server 2019, Windows Server 2025 and a Windows 11 25H2 client, in
  Clean, service-stop and Locked (VSS) acquisition states;
  (d) a self-verifying reproduction sandbox (one vagrant up re-derives the
  paper's numbers as 69 pass/fail assertions and records the run) together
  with reproduction scripts and expected outputs.
